    "body": "## Summary\n\nDraft reconstruction of ADR-081 based on the development handoff. This is a new implementation against the current `main` branch, **not a recovery of the original uncommitted local branch**.\n\n- Add `Display::InlineBlock` and route inline-block elements into inline formatting contexts.\n- Preserve nested inline-block descendants as atomic items during flattening.\n- Lay out each inline-block subtree recursively, size it atomically, and carry it through `LineFragment`.\n- Relocate nested subtree geometry into document coordinates before reusing the normal `paint_box()` path.\n- Add four layout regression tests and one Cairo paint test.\n- Add ADR-081 and update the ADR index and changelog.\n\n## Known limitations / review required\n\n- Auto-width inline-block shrink-to-fit is not implemented. Such boxes currently use available content width and may not fit side-by-side, including Wikipedia category links.\n- Baseline and `vertical-align` behavior are not implemented; initial placement is line-top based.\n- Mixed inline decorations and deeper production cases need verification.\n- The handoff reported a better Wikipedia header, intact references, and ~2.9s layout time on the prior local implementation. Those results have **not** been reproduced on this reconstructed branch.\n\n## Verification\n\n- [x] GitHub Actions Ubuntu build completed successfully.\n- [x] CTest completed successfully: 100% passed (1 CTest target, 3.42 seconds).\n- [ ] Review layout recursion and document-coordinate translation.\n- [ ] Manual Wikipedia verification (header, categories, references, dropdowns, performance).\n- [ ] Resolve any issues found before marking ready for review.\n\nThis PR remains a draft. Do not merge until manual production checks and code review are complete.",
